      en: "The Cacheu pioneer monument commemorates the first European settlers who arrived in the 15th century. It was erected in 1947 for the 500th anniversary of the Portuguese discovery of the coast of Guinea-Bissau. The monument consists of a 10-meter tall limestone obelisk with a bronze plaque. It stands on the banks of the Cacheu River, near the old town. The monument is a symbol of the colonial past and is frequently visited by tourists. It is part of the city's historical heritage.",
